{
  "_readme": ["KAN-431. Overture category -> what the app calls it.", "", "Keyed by Overture's `categories.primary`, the OPPOSITE direction from", "poiTypeCategories.json. Foursquare's tree is close to ours so that file", "maps one of ours to one of theirs; Overture has 1,357 categories in", "Portugal alone, many-to-one onto our ~124, so the key has to be theirs.", "", "`poi_type` is what a user searches. `store_kind` and `food_cuisine` are", "the subtype dimensions, and they matter: a store task cannot even be", "created without a subtype, so a `store` row with no `store_kind` is", "unreachable. Overture's finer categories are what make those subtypes", "fillable — it separates womens_clothing_store from shoe_store where its", "own coarse `basic_category` collapses both into fashion_and_apparel_store.", "", "Mapped from what the Odivelas pilot extract actually contained, ordered", "by row count, NOT from reading Overture's published taxonomy. A category", "absent here is not an error: it stays `pending` in overture_candidate", "where it can be counted, which is the whole point of staging.", "", "Deliberately unmapped, and they are the big ones: automotive_repair,", "car_dealer, dentist, hospital, medical_center, diagnostic_services.", "KAN-412 settled this — a broken car or a dentist appointment is searched", "for by name at a specific address, never stumbled upon. Pharmacy is the", "only medical errand the app needs."],
